## Run, Compile and Check

A 'mains chain' of a project runs the selected mains of one `Run`, one after the other, from the start of the first main to the end of the last one. An `OpenWithOrShortcut` running a main runs a 'mains chain' of that one main.
A 'compilation' of a project runs from the start of `Coordinator.compile` to the end of the last step of What the manager does after `Coordinator.compile`.
A project is 'busy' while a 'mains chain' or a compilation of the project runs, or a 'mains chain' of a project with a mount of the project runs.
Everything the mains of a 'mains chain' or a compilation print goes to the Output, and the Output marks where each main and the compilation start and end, and how each of them ended.
The manager keeps no Output: what a request writes in the Output goes on the connection of the request, and to the manager GUI.
A main that ends with an error, a crash included, ends the 'mains chain'.

### Files changing while a 'mains chain' runs
An 'autoCheck' that finds a project 'invalid', 'out of date' or unreachable ends every 'mains chain' that makes the project 'busy'; the Output of the project of each such 'mains chain' holds an error naming the project that changed and the main that was running.
```
A (greet.Diary->diary) in hello.mounts.
B The 'mains chain' of hello is running, at the main greet.Hello.
C The user renames the folder y2026 of diary to Y2026 with the file explorer.
D The manager GUI sends Check diary (see ManagerGuiDesign).
E The 'autoCheck' of diary at the start of that Check finds diary 'invalid'.
F The 'mains chain' of hello ends.
G The Output of hello holds an error naming diary and greet.Hello.
```

