Only T and an `EditMetadata` change reserve(M).
After a `.reconcile` of M and T, while no other program changes D, R1 to R4 (see The data in ReconciliatorDesign) hold with i = id(M) and E = captured(M), and:
```
I1  forall p in cached(M). claims(p) subset of captured(M)
```
At every moment:
```
I2  |single(D)| <= 1
```

The `replaced` of each `.reconcile` deletes the manager folder of the program of the command that `replaced` receives, when that command is inside the program folder of a manager (see Program and manager folder) and that manager folder is not the manager folder of the program calling `.reconcile`.
`replaced` deletes that manager folder only while holding the lock of the `instance.lock` of that folder (see The 'single' manager in Implementation notes).
`replaced` sends a `Quit` message to the manager folder as a 'fresh' manager process does, starting no manager process, and waits for the lock:
- On the connection of the message, the manager process sends, every 2 seconds until the manager process ends, a 'progress line': at most 80 characters saying what the manager process is doing and how much of it is done, with no time in it (`Ending the mains: 2 of 5 ended.`).
- When 10 seconds pass with no 'progress line', or with no 'progress line' different from the 'progress line' before it, `replaced` ends the manager process holding that lock.
The way a 'fresh' manager process reaches the 'single' manager, the `Quit` message and the 'progress lines' are the same for every version of the manager.

